Description: virgl/vtest: propagate connection failures to screen creation
 A missing Android vtest server must not look like a successful connection.
 Return the saved negative errno and close the socket before sending init or
 negotiating the protocol. Free the winsys on failure, and guard both software
 screen helpers against a NULL winsys (virgl_create_screen dereferences it).
 This reports screen creation failure; an explicit GALLIUM_DRIVER=virpipe
 still prevents automatic llvmpipe selection. Session fallback is separate.
Origin: vendor, Rungic
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-10-05
X-Rungic-Status: Pending [generic vtest error propagation; not submitted upstream]
X-Rungic-Tests: L0:tools/test_mesa_packaging.py (build options and series); missing-server screen creation (offline C harness; packaged EGL to verify)
X-Rungic-Docs: docs/108-husky-port.md (M5, record)
Gbp-Pq: Topic rungic

diff --git a/src/gallium/winsys/virgl/vtest/virgl_vtest_socket.c b/src/gallium/winsys/virgl/vtest/virgl_vtest_socket.c
--- a/src/gallium/winsys/virgl/vtest/virgl_vtest_socket.c
+++ b/src/gallium/winsys/virgl/vtest/virgl_vtest_socket.c
@@ -218,6 +218,13 @@
       }
    } while (ret == -EINTR);
 
+   if (ret < 0) {
+      fprintf(stderr, "vtest: failed to connect to %s: %s\n",
+              un.sun_path, strerror(-ret));
+      close(sock);
+      return ret;
+   }
+
    vws->sock_fd = sock;
    virgl_vtest_send_init(vws);
    vws->protocol_version = virgl_vtest_negotiate_version(vws, VTEST_PROTOCOL_VERSION);
diff --git a/src/gallium/winsys/virgl/vtest/virgl_vtest_winsys.c b/src/gallium/winsys/virgl/vtest/virgl_vtest_winsys.c
--- a/src/gallium/winsys/virgl/vtest/virgl_vtest_winsys.c
+++ b/src/gallium/winsys/virgl/vtest/virgl_vtest_winsys.c
@@ -780,7 +780,10 @@
    if (!vtws)
       return NULL;
 
-   virgl_vtest_connect(vtws);
+   if (virgl_vtest_connect(vtws) < 0) {
+      FREE(vtws);
+      return NULL;
+   }
    vtws->sws = sws;
 
    virgl_resource_cache_init(&vtws->cache, CACHE_TIMEOUT_USEC,
